# What `podman build` leaves out of the build context (ADR-0038). podman
# reads this with Docker's rules, not git's: a pattern without `**/` matches
# only at the top of the checkout. Build folders, keys, tool caches and
# git's own data stay out at any depth; the submodule's files stay in.
**/.git
.claude/
**/build/
**/build-*/
**/output/
**/.cache/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.venv/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/node_modules/
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
**/*.user
**/*.user.*
**/*.autosave
**/*.swp
**/.qmlls.ini
docs/brand-guide/_ds/
**/CMakeUserPresets.json
**/compile_commands.json
**/*.iso
**/*.qcow2
**/*.raw
**/*.img
**/*.tar
**/*.oci
**/*.key
**/*.pem
# A trailing `/` does not limit a pattern to folders here, so `build-*/`
# also matches the build stage's own scripts. Keep them.
!build_files/build-*.sh
